    "durationMs": 186991,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified against every requirement.\n\n**What I built** (Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21 / PostgreSQL):\n- `pom.xml` — added JPA, Flyway (core + postgres module), the PostgreSQL driver, and the boot maven plugin (the starter lacked it, so no executable jar would have been produced)\n- `App.java` — parses `DATABASE_URL` (postgresql://…) into JDBC url/username/password at startup; no credentials anywhere in config\n- `Link` entity + `LinkRepository` — JPA persistence with an atomic `UPDATE … SET clicks = clicks + 1` for exactly-once increments\n- `LinkService` — validates url (absolute http/https with host) and code (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), generates 8-char random codes, race-safe inserts via `TransactionTemplate` per attempt\n- `LinkController` + `ApiExceptionHandler` — all four endpoints, with JSON `{\"error\": …}` bodies for 404/409/422 (including malformed JSON)\n- `V1__init.sql` Flyway migration, `application.properties` (binds `0.0.0.0:8000`), executable `start.sh` (runs `java -jar target/app.jar` in the foreground; Flyway applies pending migrations during boot before Tomcat opens the port), and a README start section\n\n**Verified by HTTP tests**: 201 creates with generated and custom codes, exact URL echo, duplicate code → 409, all 422 cases (malformed JSON, missing/empty/ftp/hostless urls, short/bad-char/21-char codes, missing body), 404s, 302 with `Location` matching the stored URL, clicks incrementing exactly once per redirect, list ordering and `total`, and full data + click-count persistence across a server restart.\n\nThe test server is stopped, port 8000 is free, the test rows were removed, and the prebuilt jar is at `target/app.jar` — `sh start.sh` is ready for the grader."
